message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below. / Se você usar este repositório, cite-o como abaixo."
title: "Brazil governments fact-check and X-ray: hash-chained public data to check a viral infographic and compare what it omits"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible check of a viral infographic that compares eight Brazilian governments (1967-2026),
  plus a curated, hash-chained layer of public series (economy, money, labour, income, health,
  security, education, housing, environment, democracy) with the source edition on every row and a
  catalogue of method and rule breaks. One verdict rule is fixed in code and applied to every
  printed number; the specifications and every alternative tried are reported. A second phase adds
  a pre-registered composite index of living conditions (frozen goalposts, declared weights,
  published scenarios), a terminal of indicators with one homogeneous base per cell, a literature
  layer found by a sealed search protocol (quartile-1 studies with a named identification design)
  and the external-debt and public-debt-cost series, each as the Central Bank publishes them. No
  estimate, no score of government merit. Português: checagem reprodutível de um infográfico viral que compara oito governos
  brasileiros, mais uma camada curada de séries públicas com cadeia de hash, edição da fonte em
  cada linha e catálogo de quebras de método e de regra.
